\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O FATHER, all creating,
\par Whose wisdom, love, and power
\par First bound two lives together
\par In Eden's primal hour.
\par To-day to these thy children
\par Thine earliest gifts renew:
\par A home by Thee made happy,
\par A love by Thee kept true.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O Saviour, Guest most bounteous
\par Of old in Galilee,
\par Vouchsafe to-day Thy presence
\par With those who call on Thee;
\par Their store of earthly gladness
\par Transform to heavenly wine,
\par And teach them in the tasting
\par To know the gift is Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O Spirit of the Father,
\par Breathe on them from above,
\par So mighty in Thy pureness,
\par So tender in Thy love,
\par That, guarded by Thy presence,
\par From sin and strife kept free,
\par Their lives may own Thy guidance,
\par Their hearts be ruled by Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Except Thou build it, Father,
\par The house is built in vain;
\par Except Thou, Saviour, bless it,
\par The joy will turn to pain:
\par But nought can break the union
\par Of hearts in  Thee made one;
\par And love Thy Spirit hallows
\par Is endless love begun.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

